# Bro Code fixtures

## Canonical location

Committed Bro Code test inputs live in `test/fixtures/bro_code/*.bundle.json`.

Ingest phone / desktop exports from:
- **CAPTURE FIXTURE** (debug IMPROVE sheet) — on phone writes to app sandbox;
  on PC run `dart run tool/pull_bro_code_fixture.dart` to drop into
  `test/fixtures/bro_code/` (no clipboard). Desktop `flutter run` may write
  straight into the repo when cwd is the project root.
- **COPY DIAGNOSTIC JSON** — clipboard fallback only.
- Agent **EXPORT** — add a `fixture` block manually.

When the user says to pull the latest capture and diagnose, follow
`.cursor/rules/bro-code-pull-diagnose.mdc` (always-on): run the dart pull tool,
then diagnose the new `*.bundle.json`. Do not ask for paste.

Include `fixture.expectSyntaxOk`, `fixture.expectSandboxOk`, `fixture.improveGoal`, and `tags` when known.

## When to run

After changing Bro Code agent logic, sandbox, syntax validation, due-diligence scan, or the dev-loop capture/snapshot path:

```bash
flutter test test/bro_code_fixtures_test.dart
flutter test test/bro_code_dev_loop_test.dart
flutter test test/bro_code_improve_e2e_test.dart
```

Run full `flutter test` before merge when fixtures or agent pipeline changed.

## Fixing repro cases

1. Add or update a `*.bundle.json` with failing expectations (`expectSyntaxOk: false`, etc.).
2. Fix the coding agent, prompts, or Bro Code script.
3. Flip `fixture.expect*` to `true` once the case passes — fixtures document the baseline.

## E2E improve

`dev_loop_broken.bundle.json` + `bro_code_improve_e2e_test.dart` prove:
broken → scripted IMPROVE → verified. New failing Bro Codes: Capture Fixture, commit, keep or extend the E2E.

